WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500 align:middle line:90%

2
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.830 align:middle line:90%
Hi, this is Chase.

3
00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.080 align:middle line:84%
And I'm going to give you a
quick tour of the Calendar

4
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.670 align:middle line:90%
section in Basecamp.

5
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.670 align:middle line:84%
So let's dive in and get
started by creating an event.

6
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.970 align:middle line:90%
We just got a new client.

7
00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.535 align:middle line:84%
So I'm going to set a time for
team brainstorming session.

8
00:00:13.535 --> 00:00:14.910 align:middle line:84%
The quickest way
is just to click

9
00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.470 align:middle line:90%
on the date we want it set.

10
00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.910 align:middle line:90%
We're going to give it a name.

11
00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.530 align:middle line:84%
Since it's only one
day, we're going

12
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.372 align:middle line:90%
to leave that setting alone.

13
00:00:21.372 --> 00:00:23.580 align:middle line:84%
Then we have the option to
choose between a milestone

14
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.000 align:middle line:90%
or an event.

15
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.840 align:middle line:84%
Now, events are good markers
for meetings, travel plans,

16
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.875 align:middle line:84%
and things where you don't have
one person responsible for it.

17
00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:32.250 align:middle line:84%
Milestones are
useful for keeping

18
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.640 align:middle line:84%
track of major events, client
deliverables, or a new phase

19
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.720 align:middle line:90%
to the project.

20
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.210 align:middle line:84%
With milestones, you can
assign responsibility for them

21
00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:40.290 align:middle line:90%
to someone.

22
00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:43.200 align:middle line:84%
For us, this will be an event,
so we'll select that, and then

23
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.790 align:middle line:90%
click Add this event.

24
00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.740 align:middle line:90%
And there it is on the calendar.

25
00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.720 align:middle line:84%
You can also add to the
calendar by clicking

26
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.670 align:middle line:90%
on the Add a new event button.

27
00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.760 align:middle line:84%
In this view, you'll see
the same options as before.

28
00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.710 align:middle line:84%
If you're adding a
lot of milestones,

29
00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.470 align:middle line:84%
there's an add milestones
in bulk option as well.

30
00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:01.620 align:middle line:84%
This lets you create up to
10 milestones at a time,

31
00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.660 align:middle line:84%
while assigning due
dates and the people

32
00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.310 align:middle line:90%
responsible for completing them.

33
00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:08.438 align:middle line:84%
But what happens if your
designer calls and needs

34
00:01:08.438 --> 00:01:10.230 align:middle line:84%
to move that brainstorming
session you just

35
00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.700 align:middle line:90%
marked on the calendar?

36
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.260 align:middle line:84%
Just click on the event, change
the date, and click Save.

37
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.223 align:middle line:84%
Looking at the
entire calendar page,

38
00:01:18.223 --> 00:01:19.890 align:middle line:84%
you'll see all the
events and milestones

39
00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.620 align:middle line:84%
across the project for
the next six weeks.

40
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.390 align:middle line:84%
In the left corner,
we have a listing

41
00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.250 align:middle line:90%
of all the overdue milestones.

42
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.920 align:middle line:84%
The right corner has what's
called an agenda view, which

43
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.600 align:middle line:90%
shows three sections--

44
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.050 align:middle line:84%
overdue milestones, upcoming
events and milestones,

45
00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.930 align:middle line:84%
and past events and
completed milestones.

46
00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.780 align:middle line:84%
You can also mark milestones
as complete from this view.

47
00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.355 align:middle line:84%
Should you happen to
accidentally check one,

48
00:01:42.355 --> 00:01:43.980 align:middle line:84%
then just click on
the check mark again

49
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:47.582 align:middle line:84%
to move it back into the
upcoming milestones section.

50
00:01:47.582 --> 00:01:49.290 align:middle line:84%
So what if you want
to pull your calendar

51
00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.080 align:middle line:84%
into your own desktop
calendar program?

52
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.360 align:middle line:84%
If it's iCal compatible,
you can subscribe

53
00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.630 align:middle line:84%
to your events and milestones to
have them show on that program.

54
00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.640 align:middle line:84%
Just scroll down the
page and click the link

55
00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.380 align:middle line:90%
to subscribe to the calendar.

56
00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.990 align:middle line:84%
Then your iCal
program will appear.

57
00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.270 align:middle line:84%
My default program is
the Apple iCal one,

58
00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.070 align:middle line:90%
so that's what pops up.

59
00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:10.650 align:middle line:84%
We're going to click Subscribe
and then set these options

60
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.180 align:middle line:90%
as we want them to be.

61
00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.070 align:middle line:84%
This will add the
events to your calendar.

62
00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.200 align:middle line:84%
And from there, you can
mix them in with any others

63
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.090 align:middle line:84%
that you might have, such
as a home or work calendar.

64
00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:23.100 align:middle line:84%
It's a great way to get a quick
glance at all of your events.

65
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.110 align:middle line:84%
And that's how the
calendar feature works.

66
00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.510 align:middle line:84%
It's a great central
location for keeping track

67
00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.220 align:middle line:90%
of all those project dates.

68
00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.270 align:middle line:84%
Now it's just up to you to
make sure you don't miss them.
